From 45528d561bea640f45da4c566a6b84c8572f0528 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 22:18:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The Barrows closes: the tunnels, the chest, and a teleport
 tab

Part B, and it starts by undoing something part A got wrong. 377 already models the whole Barrows
run in varbits, and part A did not look before inventing one: %barrows_kills carries a bit per
brother, ten bits of reward potential (0..1000, which is not a coincidence), the chest's open flag
and a kill count, and %barrows carries a bit per tunnel ladder, a bit per door pair and three bits
of puzzle. So part A's %barrows_killed varp and its pack/varp.pack line are gone and the kill bits
are the cache's - read off the base var by bit number, written through the named varbit, with a
check pinning the cache's bit order against ^barrows_bit_* so the two cannot drift. Two varbits had
to be added, in %barrows's free low bits: barrows_entry_crypt and barrows_chest_paid.

The rest of that design is a gift. Every door loc is a multiloc on its own bit with a locked form
carrying NO option - which is 377's own "this one will not open", so a locked door needs no handler
and no message - the four ladders are multilocs on their chamber bit, and the chest is a multiloc
carrying Open when shut and Search and Close when open.

GETTING IN. There is no staircase down: searching a sarcophagus randomly gives the passage instead
of its brother, and the crypt that does is drawn by the first dig of a run. Six crypts and four
ladders, so the chamber is rolled on the way in and remembered by the only bit that can remember
it. Each drop tile is beside its own ladder, because the ladder's own tile is flagged blocked.

THE MAZE IS CHOSEN, NOT BUILT. Old School randomises which doors open every run and the chest must
stay reachable; a flood fill in RuneScript is not the answer, so tools/barrowsmaze.py builds the
tunnel's graph off maps/m55_151.jm2 and barrows.enum holds twenty-four masks that all leave every
ladder able to walk to the chest. One setbit_range_toint lays a whole maze, because the mask's bit
order IS the varbits' bit order. The battery re-verifies every row against the map, and checks that
all sixteen shut is NOT solvable, so the check can fail.

A door carries the player through the doorway rather than swinging, because the cache has no open
form of it. What follows them through is the wiki's table out of 128 - 12 a brother they have not
killed, 52 a skeleton, 32 a bloodworm, 32 a crypt rat - and nothing into a room already holding
eleven. After the chest has paid, every door is a brother.

REWARD POTENTIAL is the combat level of everything killed down there into a pool capped at 1000,
plus 2 a brother, which is where 1012 comes from. The brothers do not pay their combat level:
1000 + 6*2 is the only reading of that number in which a brother is worth two. The award lives in
[proc,npc_death] because the two Barrows skeletons already carry an [ai_queue3] for their drop
table and a second trigger on the same npc is a hard build error.

THE CHEST pays one roll plus one per brother to a ceiling of seven; per roll a piece of Barrows
equipment at 1/(450 - 58 * brothers) and only from a brother actually killed, or a value rolled in
1..potential read against the bands - which are the wiki's own "potential required" column and tile
1..1012 exactly as 380 + 125*5 + 6 + 1. The wiki's rates column prints coins one short of the band
its own thresholds describe; the thresholds are implemented and barrowschestspec.json says so.
Looting clears nothing - the run holds the ladder the player still has to climb - so the next dig
is what ends a run.

AND COREY'S TELEPORT TAB: obj 19629 with model 31539 out of the OSRS cache, whose 2d camera turns
out to be identical to the fourteen lectern tablets', at 1/10 on a looted chest for four to six,
landing on the tile he asked for.

Left alone: barrows_puzzle. Old School's pattern door needs an interface the 377 cache does not
have, and inventing one is not the same as importing it.

Verified: clean build, rs2check 1699 scripts / 490 configs with 0 ERROR and 0 CHECK, all eleven
batteries green, and barrows_battery.py's 436 checks against 105 mutations - each caught by its own
check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
